{"derivation":"Setup: a foreign effect is retained, then a foreign record with the same provider-native operation identity and a different record digest is retained as CONFLICTING, so the two facts form two conflict groups that list each other. The case: a third foreign record carries the first fact under a new evidence identity, so it is a DUPLICATE. LIFE-010 fixes the conflict bookkeeping: a DUPLICATE inherits the disputed value and conflict set of the retained same-fact outcome, and when that fact already conflicts with another fact, each member of the other group adds the duplicate evidence identity to its sorted conflict set; a foreign conflict list uses the same symmetric rule. The CONFLICTING row therefore lists both the original and the duplicate, the new DUPLICATE row lists the CONFLICTING record, and LIFE-006 fixes the reason set to DUPLICATE_EVIDENCE.","expected":{"budget_results":[],"decision":{"authority_result_digest":null,"decision_id":"sha256:9cf4517dcd0036faf3dd08a87042fa8a8ff1cda6cc6fe42dd88c94d47c938ee0","details":[{"classification":"DUPLICATE","evidence_id":"evidence-c2-foreign-duplicate","kind":"EFFECT"}],"disposition":"OUTCOME_RETAINED","event_digest":"sha256:41ff7c3eb5b9ed7bff116c2e2732247abe73b90967db07f691f916662ae84f5b","event_id":"effect-c2-foreign-duplicate","event_kind":"EFFECT_OBSERVED","instance_id":"case-1","permit_digest":null,"reason_codes":["DUPLICATE_EVIDENCE"],"reservation_receipt_digests":[],"schema":"seampoint.work-class/1.0.0-draft.2/decision-receipt","sequence":"4","state_after_core_digest":"sha256:aeaf256c39cb30df62ef8d5ee6954a72480157ff07d9c65bbf5e48468cf3ff69","state_before_digest":"sha256:be4d7608a6a6f6bfba6f323871e54feadc060a73d92e7b03b227f3751b7c2471"},"decision_digest":"sha256:9cf4517dcd0036faf3dd08a87042fa8a8ff1cda6cc6fe42dd88c94d47c938ee0","permit":null,"profile":"LINEAR","replay":false,"role":"LINEAR_WORK_RUNTIME","state":{"active":[{"activation_event_digest":"sha256:b8531880af944170b6df152a694fdb1fc28212d95b84ff1c3